{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0","id":70141,"title":"What news is there about Scion 2.0?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-11T16:53:10-08:00","id":70141,"title":"What news is there about Scion 2.0?","content":"It seems that I've been out of the loop for a bit (my own doing unfortunately, but I doubt anyone wants to hear why), and when I come back, everything seems to have been moved here. Now I am hearing rumors of a Scion 2.0, which is great news, but finding any information on it is proving to be a little difficult (my search-fu is weak it seems).<br /> <br /> So if anyone can either bring me up to speed on what we're expecting and when... or at least point me to a thread where this information is... that would be great! I just hope that there are plans for Print versions (outside of any Kickstarter rewards), either through LGS or Print on Demand... not big into PDFs (mostly because my PC isn't very portable).<br /> <br /> Thanks for any help in bringing me back up to speed on things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T17:59:58-08:00","id":70190,"title":"","content":"Do you mean the house rules Scion 2.0? Or do you mean Scion: Origins?<br /> <br /> I believe Scion: Origins was moved back to August 2014 and will only have a digital release. I guess a print release would be based on how many digital units they sell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T18:03:06-08:00","id":70193,"title":"","content":"While Onyx Path is out of the traditional publishing business, If you are OK with Print on Demand then you won't have issues with any of their stuff.<br /> <br /> There is little information so far on Scion 2E, because the system is still being built. However, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note\">This thread</a> is gonna be of your interest.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal\">This one</a> too, probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T22:05:09-08:00","id":70330,"title":"","content":"Here's the capsule summary:<ul><li>First four releases will be Scion: Origin (the corebook), Hero, Demigod, and God; the plan at last report was to have Origin and Hero released simultaneously.</li> <li>2e is intended to be open-ended, rather than a limited line like 1e, but they're currently focusing on getting the core books done before thinking about what comes next.</li> <li>New system descended from the Storyteller system, intended to handle power scaling from mortal to god. Still has d10s, target numbers, point-buy character creation. While many of the traits will be familiar from 1e (Legend, Virtues, Purviews, Boons), they work a bit differently. Also some new mechanics in there too.</li> <li>Origin, as the core, is aimed at playing urban fantasy games at the mortal level, and will offer a number of settings to play in. The mechanics will cover the baseline rules, as well as the rules that cover all tiers of play, such as magic and Fate. It's set to have mortals, Fate-touched mortals, pre-Visitation Scions, sorcerers, priests, oracles, and lower-tier supernaturals such as Amazons, satyrs, ghosts, vampires, and werewolves as PC options. It'll be required for the other books in the line, so 2e's likely not going to be for people who dislike having two books to play.</li> <li>Hero, Demigod and God each cover play at their respective divine tier. The idea is that each tier can be a mode of play in its own right, or can be interlinked to tell a story of divine ascension.</li> <li>Hero is set to cover ten pantheons (the six from Hero 1e, and four as yet unrevealed from around the world), going into more depth than Hero 1e; the Loa in particular are likely to be heavily changed. Also the initial set of powers you receive as a Scion post-Visitation, another set of settings, and the full mechanical concept of the scaling system, which stretches across all four core books. Also also, levelling up the various other PC options to this level, which looks to be where they top out.</li> <li>Demigod: Play in the Divine tier, introducing some new non-1e abilities. Discussion of the formation and nature of pantheons (with an eye to PCs forming their own), and how Zeus and Jupiter can be the same god, yet different. As in 1e Demigod, covering mythic locales such as terra incognitae, Touchstones, and Underworlds.</li> <li>God: Play in the Empyrean tier, with material for playing in Titan-Realms and Firmaments.</li> <li>Removing the super-long opening fiction of 1e.</li> <li>Fatebinding intended to be stronger and more player-driven, with the bindings helping to build the idea of the PC's progress towards godhood.</li> <li>Playing with 1e's cosmology, moving away from forcing the various mythological locations into Overworld/Underworld concepts (as happened with the Loa's Guinee in 1e).</li> <li>Additional pantheons may be covered in Demigod and God.</li> <li>Depending on the reception of Origin and Hero's settings, they may be detailed in further depth in future books, and/or more settings may be introduced.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T14:24:58-08:00","id":70841,"title":"","content":"So... it looks like a late 2014 release with a PoD option available soon afterwards. Looking forward to seeing the changes and what the new pantheons will be (hmmm... might have to come up with some home rules for converting the Pantheons in the Companion if they don't make the cut... shouldn't be too hard though).<br /> <br /> Looks like we might finally get some rules for making our own pantheons too... sweet! I think that was one of the major things lacking in 1e.<br /> <br /> Not too fond of the digital only format though... my PC isn't that portable (and no plans of changing that for the foreseeable future). I'm sure Onyx Path has figured out how to attract new gamers to buy their products... especially since they are unlikely to see anything in their LGS. At least a print on demand system is a fair middle ground for those of us who like holding a physical copy in their hands. Still... that is a topic for a different thread.<br /> <br /> Thanks for bringing me up to speed on one of my favorite games and its future.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:33:02-08:00","id":71009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0?p=70841#post70841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not too fond of the digital only format though... my PC isn't that portable (and no plans of changing that for the foreseeable future). I'm sure Onyx Path has figured out how to attract new gamers to buy their products... especially since they are unlikely to see anything in their LGS. At least a print on demand system is a fair middle ground for those of us who like holding a physical copy in their hands. Still... that is a topic for a different thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>WW got out of traditional print nearly four years ago. Since then everything has been released in PDF/Print-on-demand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T03:25:06-08:00","id":71139,"title":"","content":"I wasn't going to go into the whole &quot;digital debate&quot; again. I'm sure you have a marketing solution to attract new gamers who have never heard of Onyx Path or White Wolf products. I'm just one of the &quot;Old Guard&quot; who still prefers a book you can hold in your hands when gaming. At least it is nice to know that the games I love from you guys are still going strong and I will have an option for a printed version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:45:33-08:00","id":71341,"title":"","content":"You can still print the whole PDF yourself once bought <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> that's what I'll do anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T09:22:22-08:00","id":71374,"title":"","content":"The Print-on-Demand model is not significantly different from traditional publication, except that you have to order the book online instead of swinging by your local book store. You still get a physical book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T08:14:00-08:00","id":71984,"title":"","content":"As someone who was skeptical about the Print-on-Demand model (honestly just cause it was very foreign to this non-tech oriented person), I have been really pleased with it. The quality of the printing has been great, so I still get my physical copy to peruse at leisure. You are not missing out on anything with the new model and even better is that older books that were no longer in print now can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T08:39:52-08:00","id":71997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merinoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0?p=71984#post71984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who was skeptical about the Print-on-Demand model (honestly just cause it was very foreign to this non-tech oriented person), I have been really pleased with it. The quality of the printing has been great, so I still get my physical copy to peruse at leisure. You are not missing out on anything with the new model and even better is that older books that were no longer in print now can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. The premium quality printed books are very good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T07:10:04-08:00","id":74943,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if powers were ever thought to be dealt like Mage in Scion but less &quot;random&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","user":"Wickedgrail","date":". 02-19-2014, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T08:16:48-08:00","id":74973,"title":"","content":"There's been fan discussion of it, but never anything from the developers that they intend to go that route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T10:11:43-08:00","id":75040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0?p=70330#post70330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demigod: Play in the Divine tier, introducing some new non-1e abilities. Discussion of the formation and nature of pantheons (with an eye to PCs forming their own), and how Zeus and Jupiter can be the same god, yet different. As in 1e Demigod, covering mythic locales such as terra incognitae, Touchstones, and Underworlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who's made a thread on the very subject of differences between Greek gods and their Roman counterparts, colour me interested.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Playing with 1e's cosmology, moving away from forcing the various mythological locations into Overworld/Underworld concepts (as happened with the Loa's Guinee in 1e). </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear that too, since as I've said in a few other threads, I hoping to see the Korean pantheon make it into 2e, and their cosmology does NOT neatly fit in to 1e's Overworld/Underworld model, to say nothing of the NINE worlds in Norse cosmology.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/990-maplesamurai","name":"MapleSamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T17:42:48-08:00","id":75342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0?p=71009#post71009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WW got out of traditional print nearly four years ago. Since then everything has been released in PDF/Print-on-demand.</div> </div> </div> </div>PODs are fine. I haven't had a problem with PODs yet. I filled out the rest of my Scion books that way and they were all high quality.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to the release. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T00:14:36-07:00","id":125050,"title":"","content":"Is there any news about Scion 2.0? some previews? Or shall we wait for august only?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T02:20:13-07:00","id":125084,"title":"","content":"As far as I know from the Schedule page, Onyx Path just started putting it together. We'll see how far they got when August rolls around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T04:26:33-07:00","id":125116,"title":"","content":"That said, Onyx Path will be releasing Scion/Trinity's new system for community feedback sometime in May. Given it's the system for both games, we're unlikely to see anything specific to one or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T19:52:46-07:00","id":256435,"title":"","content":"Any new updates on when Scion 2.0 will be getting released?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T22:53:13-07:00","id":256536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0?p=256435#post256435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any new updates on when Scion 2.0 will be getting released?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall said at GenCon that he wanted to get the system done by the end of the year. After that, we'll see, but if he manages it, sometime into 2015 is likely for the game itself.<br /> <br /> (looks at post #18. Yeah, we blew right past that one...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T22:54:27-07:00","id":256537,"title":"","content":"Probably should try to be explicit about Scion 2E and the 'Scion 2.0' project (which really comes across more as Scion 1.5, IMO).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T09:50:35-07:00","id":256688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0?p=256537#post256537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably should try to be explicit about Scion 2E and the 'Scion 2.0' project (which really comes across more as Scion 1.5, IMO).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Scion 1.5 doesn't have as much as a ring to it, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T11:11:24-07:00","id":256711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0?p=256688#post256688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Scion 1.5 doesn't have as much as a ring to it, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Scion Extended&quot; or something like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T17:34:02-07:00","id":258588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0?p=256688#post256688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Scion 1.5 doesn't have as much as a ring to it, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's much better as a description of what '2.0' is versus 2E though. <br /> <br /> I actually thought that the &quot;Scion 2.0&quot; project *was* information about 2E for a bit until I read a lot closer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T22:28:56-07:00","id":258724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0?p=258588#post258588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's much better as a description of what '2.0' is versus 2E though.<br /> <br /> I actually thought that the &quot;Scion 2.0&quot; project *was* information about 2E for a bit until I read a lot closer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh. We actually had the name 2.0 for a long time before going public, we just happened to hit right as Scion was annoucing it's own 2nd edition. We're enough of a rules change/adjustment that we're kinda like Blood and Smoke to what Requiem is ... which is 2.0.<br /> <br /> 1.5 just makes it feel... less for us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T22:56:31-07:00","id":258753,"title":"","content":"The problem still stands that for people new to the game or to the forum, the Scion 2.0 fan project creates a certain amount of confusion with the official Scion 2e.<br /> <br /> The Scion 2.0 project is full of a lot of really good work. I'm glad it exists. But it would be good for the community to have a more straightforward way for new users to know what it is. You guys might have gotten to 2.0 first... but it doesn't really matter. It's not the official books. People needing to clarify which Scion 2 they're talking about each time gets tedious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T07:19:21-07:00","id":258960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/70141-what-news-is-there-about-scion-2-0?p=258753#post258753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem still stands that for people new to the game or to the forum, the Scion 2.0 fan project creates a certain amount of confusion with the official Scion 2e.<br /> <br /> The Scion 2.0 project is full of a lot of really good work. I'm glad it exists. But it would be good for the community to have a more straightforward way for new users to know what it is. You guys might have gotten to 2.0 first... but it doesn't really matter. It's not the official books. People needing to clarify which Scion 2 they're talking about each time gets tedious.</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually had a discussion before we released our houserules about the name and your concern did come up. It was ultimately decided to keep 2.0 as at the time Scion 2Ed was still just Scion Origins and I think there was personal attachment to the name itself.<br /> <br /> If we actually grow big enough like JSR that confusion is more rampant than our thread on the forums (and this one, though I always assume Scion 2.0 is referring to the actual game before ours) then we'll probably revist a name change to like &quot;Aynie's Awesome Adjustments.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T15:47:32-07:00","id":259316,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think we need to rush Scion 2.0 to change their names. If confusing, (it did for me), it just makes people discover what fans did for Scion and is a good thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}